iod, and payment method. All payments are non-refundable unless otherwise required by applicable law. Fees may be changed with fourteen (14) days' advance notice published on our website.</p>\n                    <p>Domains may be suspended or transferred in case of chargebacks, payment disputes, or fraudulent transactions. Services may be paused until outstanding fees are settled in full, including any applicable late fees or collection costs.</p>\n                    <p>You are solely responsible for renewing your domain before expiration. Failure to renew may result in loss of ownership, deletion of the domain from the registry, and potential registration by a third party. Domains may enter expiration and redemption cycles, during which additional fees may apply to restore the domain.</p>\n                    <p>Auto-renewal may be enabled using your selected payment method. You may opt out of auto-renewal at any time through your client portal, provided such opt-out is completed before the renewal date.  is not liable for any loss resulting from failure to renew a domain name, including losses due to expired payment methods or failed auto-renewal attempts.</p>\n                    <h3>Domain Transfers</h3>\n                    <p>Domain transfers or ownership changes require approval from both current and new registrants. Transfers may be restricted within sixty (60) days of initial registration or a prior transfer, per ICANN policy, except in limited circumstances such as court orders or disputes.</p>\n                    <p>We may act as designated agent for registrant changes when such changes are initiated through our platform. By initiating a transfer or ownership change, you authorize us to process such requests on your behalf, subject to applicable verification requirements.</p>\n                    <p>Transfers may be denied in cases of fraud, dispute, policy violation, or outstanding fees. No refunds are issued after successful transfers. The gaining registrar may require additional verification steps, and you are responsible for responding to all transfer confirmation requests within the specified timeframes.</p>\n                    <p>You must ensure that any domain to be transferred is not locked, does not have privacy protection services that would interfere with verification, and has up-to-date contact information to receive transfer authorization communications.</p>\n                    <h3>Suspension & Termination</h3>\n                    <p>This Agreement remains active until: the domain is cancelled by you; the domain is transferred to another registrar; or the domain expires without renewal. We may suspend or terminate domains for: policy violations; legal requirements; fraud or abuse; non-payment; or breach of any provision of this Agreement.</p>\n                    <p>Upon suspension or termination, all associated services may be immediately discontinued. You remain liable for all fees incurred prior to termination. No refunds apply in cases of willful violations, fraud, or conduct that jeopardizes the security or integrity of our systems or the registry.</p>\n                    <p>We may suspend privacy services in cases of abuse, fraud, legal requirement, or dispute resolution proceedings. Suspension does not relieve you of your obligation to pay all outstanding fees.</p>\n                    <p>In the event of termination, you acknowledge that we have no obligation to retain your registration data beyond any period required by ICANN or applicable law. Certain provisions of this Agreement, including those relating to indemnification, liability limitations, and dispute resolution, shall survive termination.</p>\n                    <h3>ICANN Compliance</h3>\n                    <p>You agree to comply with all applicable ICANN policies, including but not limited to the Registration Accreditation Agreement (RAA), the WHOIS Accuracy Program Specification, and any interim policies or specifications adopted by ICANN from time to time. These policies are incorporated into this Agreement by reference.</p>\n                    <p>By registering a domain, you authorize  to share required registration data with ICANN, registry operators, and legal authorities when necessary. You waive any claims related to lawful disclosure of such information as required by ICANN policy or applicable law.</p>\n                    <p>ICANN may conduct compliance audits, and you agree to cooperate fully with any such audit. We may be required to verify your contact information periodically, and you consent to receiving verification notices and responding to them within the specified timeframes.</p>\n                    <p>If you fail to comply with ICANN-mandated verification requests, your domain may be suspended or cancelled in accordance with ICANN policy. We shall not be liable for any loss arising from such suspension or cancellation when undertaken to comply with ICANN requirements.</p>\n                    <h3>Dispute Resolution (UDRP)</h3>\n                    <p>You agree to comply with ICANN's Uniform Domain Name Dispute Resolution Policy (UDRP) and any applicable registry dispute procedures. The UDRP is incorporated into this Agreement by reference and is available at <a href=\"https://www.icann.org/resources/pages/help/dndr/udrp-en\" target=\"_blank\">www.icann.org</a>.</p>\n                    <p> may suspend, lock, or transfer domains involved in disputes or legal proceedings at the direction of a court, arbitration panel, or approved dispute resolution provider. We are not a party to any dispute between you and a third party regarding domain ownership or use.</p>\n                    <p>You agree to submit to the jurisdiction of the courts located in the jurisdiction of our principal place of business for the resolution of any dispute not subject to the UDRP or other mandatory dispute resolution policy. You further agree that any legal action arising from this Agreement 